From d4d29108a5fb80e0973eb8cae93f397ee8919147 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Downstream Patch Queue <downstream@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:02:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 27/29] Remove the API live reporting module from the product

Cut the live reporting (Settings -> API) module at its integration seams on
all three platforms instead of deleting its engine sources.

macOS: the settings window builds tabs from a filtered pane list, the menu
bar dashboard no longer offers the reporting invitation or footer indicator,
and AppModel.activate(live:) no longer activates the ReportController.

Windows: the settings navigation no longer lists the report page, and the
report controller is never started and never attaches dashboard surfaces.

Linux: the ReportController object and all of its settings, tray, preview and
consent wiring are removed; the API page leaves the settings stack and the
dashboard drops the invitation card and reporting indicator.

The reporting engine (macOS Sources/AgentSpeed/Reporting, Windows
Reporting/*, Linux core/src/report) and its view files stay in the tree so
the queue keeps rebasing cleanly.
